{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","title":"lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":279,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-expmap]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","line":767,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[the exponential map traces geodesic rays]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch3-expmap, lem:dc-ch3-2-6}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:after-2.8}\n  For $v\\in T_pM$ and $t$ in the maximal interval of the geodesic with initial\n  data $(p,v)$,\n  $$\\exp_p(t\\,v)=\\gamma(t,p,v).$$\n  In particular $t\\mapsto\\exp_p(t\\,v)$ \\emph{is} the geodesic through $p$ with\n  initial velocity $v$; this is the computational heart of\n  $d(\\exp_p)_0=\\mathrm{id}$ in \\cref{prop:dc-ch3-2-9}.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  For $t=0$ both sides are $p$. For $t\\neq0$ this is the homogeneity\n  $\\gamma(1,p,t\\,v)=\\gamma(t\\cdot 1,p,v)$ of \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-2-6} evaluated at\n  time $1$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[the exponential map traces geodesic rays] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d6578706d61702d726179\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23def%3Adc-ch3-expmap\">↗ def:dc-ch3-expmap</a> <a class=\"wikilink